+\begin{remark}[Machine-checked linear strengthening]\label{rem:rocq}
+After the proof above was written and human-reviewed, Conjecture~1.15 was formalized in Rocq/MathComp in the companion repository \href{https://github.com/graph-theory-AI/graph-theory-rocq}{graph-theory-AI/graph-theory-rocq}. The theorem \href{https://github.com/graph-theory-AI/graph-theory-rocq/blob/main/packing-theory/theories/foundations/fair_matching.v}{\texttt{x15\_llm3\_proof}} proves the stronger bound $c(m)\le12m+14$ and reports no added axioms. The formal proof starts from Kőnig line colouring and a two-way splitting-necklace interpolation, but replaces the Carathéodory reduction and one-interpolation-per-pair scheme used here by synchronized rounds: all pairs in one level of the mixing tree share a single necklace splitting. Retyping one bead of each odd class type makes each class count round down exactly, so the final trimming phase also disappears. These changes, suggested by Laurent Viennot, reduce the bound from cubic to linear in $m$. The companion repository documents the correspondence with Conjecture~1.15 but, at the time of this update, marks its independent source-correspondence review as pending.
+\end{remark}
+
 \begin{remark}[Slack recorded by the referee]\label{rem:slack}
